From 831e1db5dadb43a88d430ffa3a9db2e21b5b3af2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex Executor <codex-executor@local>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 19:44:29 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 23/24] sheet route: sparse symmetric assembled solve in the
 block validation, support mask and numerical rank in the label, panel results

The block validation held the assembled carrier operator as a dense matrix and took its full eigendecomposition
(65 GB for 3 x 3 x 2), which took the machine down twice; it is now block sparse, factorised by symmetric Pardiso on
the upper triangle (in-core when it fits), the four smallest eigenvalues by shift-invert.  2 x 2 x 2 and 3 x 3 x 2
coarse panels with the repaired labels: assembly error on service loads below 1e-3 at both sizes, interface
displacement error not growing; the 2 x 2 x 2 assembly error fell by 3x to 200x with the sliver fix.

Every label now ships support_mask, numerical_rank at 1e-14 and 1e-10 lambda_max and rank_thresholds, and the
receipt schur.support (decision of record: the null space is a lower bound and there is no spectral gap).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01X77H1Uihff2oEyM5T4qg7v
